<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Monteagle year share rises, dividend up.</title>
<headline>Monteagle year share rises, dividend up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     22.58    vs   10.45</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  8.00    vs    7.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    1.48    vs    0.68</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    3.09    vs    2.16</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.89    vs    0.95</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    1.78    vs    1.44</p>
<p>    Turnover		  32.98    vs   28.15</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	1.25    vs    0.39 loss</p>
<p>Div payable: May 10</p>
<p>on register: March 28</p>
<p>Full name: Monteagle Societe Anonyme</p>
<p>NOTE - There was a net credit from exceptional items following recovery of depreciation in the value of properties in the U.S. and certain portfolio realisations during the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
